#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Larkspur Hall: a tile-based comedy of a week below stairs in a country
house, in Python + Tk.

Standard library only.  The engine is the one Miskatonic, Hyperspace
Homeroom, Clover Vale, Lazarus Deep and Penultimate share (one hero, a map
of squares, people to talk to by keyword, a shop, places underneath), and
the rules are those of Maid RPG: six Attributes rolled on two dice and
divided by three, Maid Types, Special Qualities, Maid Roots and a Maid
Power, all rolled on the tables; every roll a single die times an
Attribute; Stress that piles up until you have a Stress Explosion; and
Favor, which is how pleased the Master is with you, and which you can spend.

Larkspur Hall, a rambling country house with too many rooms and not enough
maids.  You are the newest of them.  The Master's birthday is in seven days,
and the Master doesn't want a party.  The Master's great-aunt, the Dowager,
who holds the family purse, is coming on the day itself to decide whether
Larkspur carries on as it is, or is sold, and its household turned out.
And since the night you arrived, someone calling themselves the Phantom of
Larkspur has been leaving calling cards, and taking things.

Who the Phantom is, what the Master wishes for, and which maid the Master
will thank most at the end of the week, are for you to find out.

Every new game makes a new household: a new Master (rolled on the Master
tables), new fellow maids (rolled on the maid tables, like you), a new
Phantom, and new places for things to be hidden.  The game is saved to
~/.larkspur.json whenever you change place and when you quit, and resumed
next time.

Rolls
  Roll a die and multiply it by the Attribute you're using (Athletics,
  Affection, Skill, Cunning, Luck or Will): beat the difficulty, 4 to 10.
  At 0 in an Attribute you can't succeed at all.  Every piece of your
  uniform that's dirty, torn or missing takes 1 off the die (the headdress
  2).

Contests
  When you're up against someone (a goose, a rival, the Phantom), you both
  roll, each with the Attribute you choose to use.  The loser takes Stress:
  the winner's total divided by the loser's Attribute.

Stress and Favor
  When your Stress goes over your Spirit (Will x 10) you have a Stress
  Explosion, and until it drains away (a point a minute) you can only do
  what your Explosion says.  Favor comes from the Master, for chores done
  (1d6), a nice moment together (2d6), troubles put right (2d6 to 3d6) and
  saving the day (3d6 or more).  Spend it to shed Stress, to try harder
  (+1 to a die), to raise an Attribute, or to make a Random Event happen.
  Below zero, you're dismissed.

Talking
  Walk into someone, then choose or type a word.  Everyone knows NAME, JOB
  and BYE; most know NEWS, and words in CAPITALS are worth asking about.
  The grocer answers BUY.  Ask the Master to COME for a walk.  Words like
  PHANTOM, WISH and CAKE are worth asking everyone.

Touch and mouse
  Tap a square to walk there, tap next to you to step, and tap the menus.
  Gamepad (Linux, the Steam Deck): the d-pad or stick moves, A waits or
  chooses, B backs out, X does the nearest chore, Y spends Favor, LB uses
  something, RB the journal, View the map and Start the menu.

Sound effects and music are synthesized and played with afplay (macOS),
paplay or aplay if one is available, on Android with pyjnius, or with
pygame's mixer; otherwise the game is silent.  Music is cached in
~/.cache/larkspur.

App bundle (macOS):  larkspur --build-app [DIR]   builds larkspur.app
                     larkspur --icon-png SIZE [OUT.png]

Keys
  Arrows/WASD move, Space waits, E searches, C does a chore here, F spends
  Favor, U uses something, I shows your maid, J the journal, R the rota, M
  the map, Z waits until something happens, ? help.

The tiles are drawn by the code below (MAID_SHAPE, PERSON_SHAPES, ART and
draw_terrain).  --selftest builds every map, room, level and tune of a few
households without opening a window.
"""

